# EduConnect — Backend

FastAPI + PostgreSQL backend for the EduConnect platform: multi-institution
student registration, career roadmaps (Groq AI), a full LMS (courses, quizzes,
assignments, certificates), and a super-admin / college-admin institution
management layer.

## Tech stack

- *FastAPI* + *Pydantic v2* — API layer
- *SQLAlchemy 2.0* + *Alembic* — ORM and migrations
- *PostgreSQL 15+* — database (SQLite is used only by the automated tests)
- *Argon2* (pwdlib) — password hashing
- *PyJWT* — access/refresh token auth
- *Groq* — AI roadmap generation and resume parsing
- *ReportLab* + *qrcode* — certificate PDF generation

## Prerequisites

- Python 3.12+
- PostgreSQL 15+ running locally (or a connection string to a hosted instance)
- (Optional) A [Groq API key](https://console.groq.com) — only needed for AI
  roadmap generation and the ATS resume builder. Everything else works without it.

## 1. Install dependencies

bash
cd backend
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate      # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt --break-system-packages   # drop the flag if not needed on your OS


## 2. Configure environment

bash
cp .env.example .env


Windows (PowerShell): Copy-Item .env.example .env

Edit .env and set at minimum:

| Variable | What it's for |
|---|---|
| DATABASE_URL | PostgreSQL connection string, e.g. postgresql+psycopg://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/educonnect |
| JWT_SECRET | Long random string — *must* be changed before any real deployment |
| CORS_ORIGINS | Frontend origin(s), comma-separated. Defaults to http://localhost:5173 |
| GROQ_API_KEY | Only required for AI roadmap generation / resume builder |

Create the database itself (once) if it doesn't already exist:

bash
createdb educonnect


## 3. Run migrations

bash
alembic upgrade head


This creates every table — institutions, users, courses, quizzes, assignments,
certificates, the resume builder, and the institution approval workflow.

## 4. Seed data

*Master data* (a starter set of colleges & programs, used by the student
registration dropdowns):

bash
python -m scripts.seed_masters


*Platform owner account* (super_admin — approves/rejects/suspends
institutions):

*macOS/Linux:*
bash
SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL=owner@educonnect.dev \
SUPER_ADMIN_PASSWORD=ReplaceWithStrongPassword123 \
SUPER_ADMIN_MOBILE=9876500000 \
python -m scripts.seed_super_admin


*Windows (PowerShell):*
powershell
$env:SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL="owner@educonnect.dev"
$env:SUPER_ADMIN_PASSWORD="ReplaceWithStrongPassword123"
$env:SUPER_ADMIN_MOBILE="9876500000"
python -m scripts.seed_super_admin


There is no public sign-up for this role by design — it's always seeded
directly against the database. The script is idempotent; re-running it with a
new password just rotates the credentials.

*A standalone college admin* (optional — normally an institution's first
admin is created automatically when they register via
POST /api/v1/institutions/register and approved by the super admin; use
this script only if you need a global admin outside that flow):

*macOS/Linux:*
bash
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com \
ADMIN_PASSWORD=ReplaceWithStrongPassword123 \
ADMIN_MOBILE=9876543210 \
python -m scripts.create_admin


*Windows (PowerShell):*
powershell
$env:ADMIN_EMAIL="admin@example.com"
$env:ADMIN_PASSWORD="ReplaceWithStrongPassword123"
$env:ADMIN_MOBILE="9876543210"
python -m scripts.create_admin

## 5. Run the server

bash
uvicorn app.main:app --reload


The API is now at http://localhost:8000. Interactive docs (Swagger UI) are
at http://localhost:8000/docs.

## Running tests

bash
pytest


Tests run against an in-memory SQLite database and don't touch your real
Postgres instance — no extra setup needed.

## Project structure


app/
  main.py                    Auth (student/admin login), root student endpoints
  models.py                  All SQLAlchemy models
  dependencies.py            get_current_student / get_current_admin / get_current_super_admin
  config.py                  Settings (reads .env)

  institution_router.py      Public college registration + super-admin approve/reject/suspend
  college_portal_router.py   College admin's own institution profile/programs/students

  career_router.py           Skills, goals, roadmap generation, course catalog, enrollment
  roadmap_service.py         Groq-powered roadmap + course matching
  resume_service.py          Resume text extraction (PDF/DOCX)
  resume_builder_router.py   ATS resume builder (auto-syncs completed courses)

  admin_course_router.py     Course/section/lesson CRUD, publish/archive, analytics
  quiz_router.py             Quiz builder (admin) + quiz attempts (student)
  assignment_router.py       Assignment builder, submissions, evaluation, my-assignments
  certificate_router.py      Certificate issue/revoke/reissue + public verification
  analytics_router.py        Student learning dashboard / progress

scripts/
  seed_masters.py            Seed starter colleges & programs
  seed_super_admin.py        Create/promote the platform-owner account
  create_admin.py            Create a standalone (non-institution-scoped) admin

alembic/versions/            One migration per feature, run in order
tests/                       pytest suite (SQLite, no external services needed)


## Roles

| Role | Created via | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| student | Self-registration (/auth/student/register) | Their own account, their institution's offered programs |
| admin (college admin) | Institution registration → super-admin approval | Their own institution only — courses, students, quizzes, certificates, institution profile |
| super_admin | scripts/seed_super_admin.py only | Every institution — approve/reject/suspend |

Both admin and super_admin log in through the same endpoint
(POST /api/v1/auth/admin/login); the frontend calls
GET /api/v1/auth/staff/role right after login to route to the correct
dashboard.